id: pm-github-z5z1
title: Let reusable sync choose its npm project directory
description: "GitHub issue: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/129. Add optional npm-project-dir (default .), validate a repository-contained npm project before installation, and use it for dependencies, CLI PATH, and the caller post-import script without expanding the publication allowlist."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-15T17:57:16.378Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T20:00:59.345Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T17:57:29.182Z",codex-agent,"Design: validate npm-project-dir after checkout and before setup-node caching or npm install; reject absolute/traversal paths, resolved symlink escapes, missing package.json, and environment/PATH separators with one named-input diagnostic. Export the canonical project path for install, PATH and the post-import script; resolve the SDK there while keeping tracker and Git operations at the repository root. Preserve the publication allowlist. Contract tests execute shell extracted from the real workflow with real temporary projects; perform and record a behavioral revert per regression scenario."
  "2026-10-15T18:05:04.398Z",codex-agent,"Focused acceptance: all 12 npm-project-dir tests pass (zero fail/skip/cancel/todo), including real npm ci with ignored lifecycle scripts, byte-identical legacy default PATH/script receipts, and a real pinned CLI/SDK plus packed extension publishing one imported issue from tests/oracle with no root package.json or nested tracker. Publication remains restricted to the root tracker and root CHANGELOG.md. Cache discovery follows the selected project and accepts npm lockfile or shrinkwrap."
  "2026-10-15T18:05:05.519Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (workflow shell only changed; tests unchanged, no rebuild needed): default test fails 1/1 when its declared default points to a missing directory. Subdirectory install/PATH/script test fails 1/1 independently when each corresponding command is restored to the old root behavior (3 runs). Each refusal test fails when validation is reverted to accepting the root unconditionally: parent, embedded-parent, absolute, missing-package, missing-directory, symlink-escape, newline, colon, empty (9/9 fail, 0 pass). Full subdirectory publication test fails 1/1 with only SDK resolution reverted, and 1/1 with only CLI invocations reverted (2 runs). All seven controls exited 1 with the expected failures; restored the implementation after every run."
  "2026-10-15T18:05:06.631Z",codex-agent,"PM CLI UX gaps: linked-test command edits are refused by --set-json and require remove/re-add; pm test --run --progress passed 12/12 but reported evidence_recording=tracking_disabled, so the receipt is recorded in this comment without changing project policy. Fixture execution must explicitly prepend the package-pinned CLI to PATH; otherwise global CLI drift can alter generated merge attributes."
  "2026-10-15T18:27:06.041Z",codex-agent,"Review found a symlink edge case: command substitution strips trailing newlines from a canonical path and could validate a sibling containing package.json instead of the symlink target. Added a regression using a newline-ending target without a manifest and a sibling with one; it fails against the initial validator. Read realpath's NUL-terminated output with Bash read so separators remain visible and are rejected. Stopped the initial npm gate without claiming a result; restarting the required gates on the final implementation."
  "2026-10-15T18:29:03.029Z",codex-agent,"Final focused acceptance: pm test --run --progress passes 13/13 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled/todo. Refreshed all controls against the final workflow and unchanged final tests: default mutation 1 expected failure; install cwd, PATH, post-import cwd reverts each 1; validation bypass 10/10 refusal failures (including symlink-newline-target); SDK revert 1; CLI revert 1; NUL-read-only revert 1. All 8 controls exited 1 with 17 expected failures total, zero unexpected passes. Restored the workflow after each control."
  "2026-10-15T19:02:01.733Z",codex-agent,"The npm release gate completed 675/676 tests with one failure in the existing workflow publication-auditor self-test: pm-ops misread the parenthesized Bash traversal regex as publish invocations. Replaced only that traversal check with an equivalent Bash case path-segment pattern; kept the canonical NUL read and separator checks. The auditor itself and all thresholds remain unchanged. Direct attestation verification now passes, and the combined feature plus repository-auditor focused run passes 14/14. The earlier gate is failed evidence, not a green receipt; rerunning both required gates on this final syntax."
  "2026-10-15T19:03:46.803Z",codex-agent,"Final case-pattern implementation: refreshed all 9 controls against unchanged final tests. Expected failures: default mutation 1; install/PATH/script reverts 1 each; validation bypass 10; SDK revert 1; CLI revert 1; NUL-read revert 1; case-check-only revert to grouped regex 1 in the existing repository-auditor test. Total 18 expected failures, zero unexpected passes; workflow restored after every run. All 8 attestation tests pass with the final syntax."
  "2026-10-15T19:06:43.317Z",codex-agent,"Final syntax preflight: linked feature suite 13/13 and linked attestation suite 8/8 pass through pm test --run --progress. Typecheck, build, docstrings (12 files, 158 declarations), lint, duplication (13 authored modules, 10036 lines, zero duplicates), privacy (4453 objects), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog regeneration/check and direct publication attestation all pass. Starting fresh npm and Bun release:check runs with clean HOME and no global/system Git config."
  "2026-10-15T20:00:57.101Z",codex-agent,"Final delivery gates passed on the final implementation: npm run release:check exit 0 and bun run release:check exit 0, each with a fresh HOME and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Both ran 676/676 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Each measured 13 authored modules with exact 10040/10040 lines, 10040/10040 statements, 255/255 functions and 2832/2832 branches; no skipped source. Thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged. Docstrings 12 files/158 declarations; duplication zero across 13 modules/10036 lines; privacy 4453 objects approved; production audit zero vulnerabilities; package dry-run, changelog and publication-attestation checks pass."
  "2026-10-15T20:00:58.048Z",codex-agent,"Implementation, caller documentation, 13 feature tests, 8 attestation tests and all 9 behavioral controls (18 expected failures) are complete. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review; the item remains nonterminal. Remaining boundary: hosted PR checks and a released/caller-repinned workflow are not established by these local gates. PM CLI gaps encountered are documented above; no upstream CLI reports were filed."
